🌐 EasyStack
Bringing Stacks to Everyone — Simple, Social, and Seamless
EasyStack


🚀 Overview

EasyStack is a new kind of staking & engagement platform built on the Stacks blockchain — designed to make Web3 accessible to everyone, especially Web2 users.

At its core, EasyStack lets users stake tokens, earn rewards, and unlock “quest points” for community and ecosystem participation — all through a simple, wallet-free experience powered by embedded wallets (via Turnkey).

Think of it as the foundation for mainstream Stacks onboarding — a bridge between traditional users who want simplicity, and the Stacks ecosystem that values decentralization.

🧱 The Foundation — What We’ve Built So Far
Core Contract: easystack.clar

The current version of EasyStack introduces the on-chain foundation:

✅ User registration & profile mapping

✅ Token staking & tracking (STX)

✅ Reward distribution logic

✅ Claim intervals using block-height

✅ Quest point mechanics for early engagement

✅ Claim rate variables & dynamic reward adjustments

The smart contract is fully modular, meaning future upgrades like NFTs, social badges, or fiat gateways can connect without breaking current logic.

Token Contract: easy-token.clar

Implements a simple fungible token with mint/burn logic.

Used to issue rewards and incentives to stakers.

Designed to be extended into a utility/reputation token.

💡 Vision — Where We’re Headed

EasyStack isn’t just a staking platform — it’s the base layer of a social-financial network on Stacks.

🌍 Our Goals

Seamless Onboarding:
Users can sign in with email or social login — no wallet setup or seed phrases needed, thanks to Turnkey Embedded Wallets.

Fiat-to-STX Onramp:
Enable users to pay or top-up in fiat (USD, NGN, etc.) using cards or bank transfers, abstracting away crypto complexity.

Gamified Ecosystem:
Introduce quests, achievements, and XP systems tied to on-chain actions (staking, referrals, project contributions).

Web2 + Web3 Integration:
Blend familiar Web2 UX (Next.js frontend, Supabase backend, smooth auth) with Stacks smart contract logic underneath.

Community-Centric Growth:
Users don’t just stake — they grow their influence in the Stacks community via transparent, measurable engagement.

🧩 Tech Stack
Layer	Technology	Description
Smart Contracts	Clarity (Stacks)	On-chain staking, reward, and quest logic
Frontend	Next.js, TailwindCSS	Modern, performant UI with easy user flow
Wallet/Auth	Turnkey Embedded Wallets	Seamless Web2-style onboarding
User profiles, off-chain metadata, API routes
Deployment	Vercel	Fast CI/CD for frontend and API hosting
Blockchain	Stacks (secured by Bitcoin)	Decentralized settlement layer
🧭 Roadmap
Phase	Stage	Description
🏗️ Phase 1 — Foundation	✅ Completed	Core staking & rewards contract, token deployment, Clarinet setup
🔗 Phase 2 — Embedded Wallet Integration	🚧 In Progress	Turnkey wallet connection, email/social login
💳 Phase 3 — Fiat Gateway	⏳ Upcoming	Pay in fiat → get STX or EasyTokens
🎮 Phase 4 — Gamified Quests	Planned	On-chain quest rewards, leaderboard, and NFT badges
🪩 Phase 5 — Public Launch	Planned	Open registration, community staking pools, governance
🧰 Local Setup


# Install Clarinet
brew install clarinet

# Check contracts
clarinet check

# Run tests
clarinet test


Frontend and API integration instructions will be added once the Turnkey auth layer is merged.

🧠 Philosophy

“Web3 will only scale when users stop realizing they’re using Web3.”

EasyStack is built around invisible blockchain UX — users come for the utility, not the technology.
The mission: make Stacks adoption as easy as signing in with Google or buying coffee with a card.

